// A library reached by two import paths is checked once (ADR 9.10.26p):
// `left` and `right` both declare `base`, so the walk elaborates `base.tg`
// twice and records two copies of `base_refl`. The kernel treats one file's
// copies as one definition, checks each, and admits the diamond. The
// definition count still counts `base` twice — that is module identity's,
// not this ADR's (its § 3).

mod left;
mod right;
